    "turn_text": "See, every time I make a line, I have to look at that line I want to make and go, it's my job to report on things going on. It's my job to commentate commentary on everything going on. That's my job. And there are no sacred cows, myself included. Especially people who are in the public eye, put themselves in the public eye. Rarely does somebody enter the public eye that doesn't want to be there. If they are in the public eye against their well, chances are there's a trial going on. So in talking about the former Boise City Councilwoman, I had a moment today where I passed up on another headline of hers, another story of hers a couple of days ago because I had pretty much already had a go at her, right? I don't need to kick this horse too many times. It's having a bad time. It's already down. All right. I mean, I could. I could very easily. But I didn't, my choice. I have another, I have another story, I've got a couple stories. And I, I'm hesitant to plan because I actually fear now, I fear that Miss Sanchez might be near the brink. and it's fun and entertaining when somebody is saying and doing something stupid right that that's fun and entertaining when somebody says or does something amazingly stupid fair game but i don't want anyone to be physically hurt i don't want anyone to be to to feel like they're bullied and i definitely don't want anyone to take matters into their own hands and and do something about it. So I found myself and I was wondering, Hmm, could we be could I be close? Could she be close to that point? And we just don't know it yet? Because right now Lisa Sanchez, who I believe to have a number of mental health issues. It's not my belief. She said she's had them. She's having an episode. I think she might actually be having a very public episode. And I want Miss Sanchez to lead a long fruitful life, hopefully with no say so in how I live mine, but just go ahead. Be happy. Go somewhere. Do something. Be happy. Make a living. Be happy. She's suing the city of Boise. She's suing the city of Boise because she wants a judge to remove her replacement that city council voted on and the mayor approved.",
